node_modules/
out/
release/
dist/
resources/bin/

# Local verification secrets. Never commit an API key: git history is permanent and a key
# pushed once must be treated as burned even if the next commit removes it.
.secrets/
*.local.json
.env
.env.*

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Engineering process — private, never published (tester decision, 2026-10-17).
#
# The workflow and planning material stays on this machine and out of the repository: agent rules
# and prompts, the planning documents, the fork's design notes and the research scripts. The one
# document meant for developers is ARCHITECTURE.md, which stays tracked; README.md, CHANGELOG.md,
# LICENSE, THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md, licenses/ and vendor/ are product files and stay tracked too.
#
# These files were tracked until 2026-10-17, so older local commits still hold them. They must be
# removed from whatever history is published; see the release checklist kept with the plans.
# Untracked means no git history: the round backup zips are their only copies.
AGENTS.md
SETUP.md
docs/
design/
.cursor/
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Third-party reference material: the gemini-srt-translator source and the Kodi addon whose
# gender-oracle algorithm NG plans to port. Kept out of the repository because it is upstream
# code that is re-downloadable, not ours to republish as though it were. It IS required reading
# for the planner, so it stays on disk — see .cursor/plans/handoff.md §7.
Source Codes/

*.log
*.tsbuildinfo
__pycache__/
.DS_Store
.vite/

# Probe scratch: generated media fixtures and the console logs of the runs made on them.
# Large, regenerable, and never part of a build. Covered by a pattern rather than by name
# because each probe makes its own, and they are normally deleted on success — so the one that
# survives is the one whose probe crashed, which is exactly when nobody is thinking about
# .gitignore.
.tmp-*/

# Private evaluation material. `.cursor/exports/` holds review packages built for the tester:
# full copyrighted subtitle files, raw request/response dumps and private zips. The review
# snippets are excerpts of the same material. Neither may enter history, which is permanent.
# `.vscode/` is per-machine editor state. The `.diff` is a raw comparison of third-party add-on
# source taken from `Source Codes/`, which is excluded for the reason given above it.
.cursor/exports/
.cursor/tools/_f15_review_snip*.txt
.cursor/tools/f15_subsync_*.diff
.vscode/
